# WolkaraForever patch 0079: ordered committed Unicode input.
#
# The iPhone cn.7 trace observed F12 and Return twice, with focused SAY input,
# but zero non-empty text changes/API calls. Both user messages were Chinese.
# UIKit commits unmapped Unicode, while the old host emitted raw key code 0xFF
# pairs. A raw-key client can ignore those without ever asking to interpret text.
# Retain these commits in the existing event queue and deliver once through the
# public NSTextInputClient interface, after preceding keys, before Return.
# No game code, send API, raw input logging, retries or arbitrary key remapping.
# Existing ASCII/control key handling and physical key events keep their route.
#
# Foundation fixture: modern/legacy clients, once-only delivery, copied text,
# unavailable client, metadata-only logs and a raw-key client that rejects 0xFF.
# Both polling and NSApplication-owned dispatch consume the private event.
# Applies after 0078; platform/ stays byte-identical to its pinned upstream.
# Upstream: candidate. Chinese input/send/self-echo/display confirmed by a user
# test and saved metadata on iPhone 17, Developer service, 2026-11-23.
#
